 +10 | about +6 | Close to ideal |\n| 2 | about +11 | about +12 | Close to ideal |\n\n- **Candidate 4:** ordering every day saves about 546 in storage, but 28 order fees cost 504 more. That nets only about +40, which its surplus wipes out.\n- **Candidate 5:** ordering every 3 days saves about 110–140 in fees. But the stock it carries between deliveries costs about 570 more in storage, and on day 11 it may exceed capacity.\n- **Candidate 7:** being short costs about 700 on product 0 and about 400 on product 1. Overall it comes out worse than candidate 6.\n\n**Candidate 2 vs Candidate 6.** Both order every 2 days and track expected demand closely, with small cuts in the last orders. Candidate 2 makes one small order on day 0 that covers only day 2, then switches to odd-day orders.\n- **Fees:** that costs one extra order fee (+36).\n- **Storage:** its 2-day blocks fall differently, so less stock sits overnight, including day 11's 90-unit demand peak. That saves about 81 on product 0 and about 20 on product 1.\n- **Net:** about +65 for candidate 2. Its slightly larger margin on product 1 is about neutral.\n\n**Randomness:** both plans hold a similar safety margin at the start and take on similar risk. Neither has the large surpluses that make candidates 0, 1, 3 and 4 fragile."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6146, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 6146}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T00:15:54.004Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPt8GsYNSGwurhZvyWu5"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"